# Ruling 2025-07-25: "Any 'enters with' abilities of the copied permanent will also work", and the copy does not copy counters.
# Bot1's Walking Ballista (cast for X=2 on turn 1, two +1/+1 counters) is copied by Devastating Onslaught: the token's "enters
# with X +1/+1 counters" has X = 0 (CR 107.3g, the token was never cast), so it enters as a 0/0 and dies as a state-based action
# (CR 704.5f). The original keeps its two counters. Had the token copied the counters it would have lived to the end step.
# LeftBattlefield records the token's one trip, so a token really was created.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Walking Ballista
Devastating Onslaught
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Devastating Onslaught.Cast(Walking Ballista; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
? LeftBattlefield.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Sapphire; Mox Emerald; Walking Ballista
Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = Devastating Onslaught
LeftBattlefield.Count = 1
